Case 1: the reported queries -- GROUP BY on t_a alone, and the same with a one-row cross join     

===================================================
g    cnt    
1     2     
2     2     
3     2     

Query plan:
iscan
    class: a node[?]
    index: i_a_g (covers)
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select a.g, count(*) from t_a a group by a.g using index a.i_a_g
/* ---> skip GROUP BY */
===================================================
g    cnt    
1     2     
2     2     
3     2     

Query plan:
nl-join (cross join)
    outer: iscan
               class: a node[?]
               index: i_a_g (covers)
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: sscan
               class: o node[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select a.g, count(*) from t_a a, t_one o group by a.g using index a.i_a_g
/* ---> skip GROUP BY */
===================================================
    
Case 2: an inner join under a cross join, the index of t_a is two joins down     

===================================================
g    cnt    
1     3     
2     2     
3     2     

Query plan:
nl-join (cross join)
    outer: idx-join (inner join)
               outer: iscan
                          class: a node[?]
                          index: i_a_g 
                          cost:  ? card ?
               inner: iscan
                          class: b node[?]
                          index: i_b_aid term[?] (covers)
                          cost:  ? card ?
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: sscan
               class: o node[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ ORDERED USE_IDX */ a.g, count(*) from t_a a, t_b b, t_one o where b.a_id=a.id group by a.g using index a.i_a_g, b.i_b_aid
/* ---> skip GROUP BY */
===================================================
    
Case 3: left outer join, a t_a row without a match in t_b is counted in its group     

===================================================
g    cnt    cnt_b    
1     3     3     
2     3     2     
3     2     2     

Query plan:
idx-join (left outer join)
    outer: iscan
               class: a node[?]
               index: i_a_g 
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: iscan
               class: b node[?]
               index: i_b_aid term[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ USE_IDX */ a.g, count(*), count(b.id) from t_a a left outer join t_b b on b.a_id=a.id group by a.g using index a.i_a_g, b.i_b_aid
/* ---> skip GROUP BY */
===================================================
    
Case 4: hash join, the GROUP BY is still sorted     

===================================================
g    cnt    
1     3     
2     2     
3     2     

Query plan:
temp(group by)
    subplan: hash-join (inner join)
                 edge:  term[?]
                 outer: iscan
                            class: a node[?]
                            index: i_a_g 
                            cost:  ? card ?
                 inner: sscan
                            class: b node[?]
                            cost:  ? card ?
                 cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ ORDERED USE_HASH */ a.g, count(*) from t_a a, t_b b where b.a_id=a.id group by a.g using index a.i_a_g, b.i_b_aid
